{'symbol': 'LLY', 'date': '2020-08-04 14:30:00', 'title': 'NIH LAUNCHES CLINICAL TRIAL TO TEST ANTIBODY TREATMENT IN HOSPITALIZED COVID-19 PATIENTS', 'text': 'NIH LAUNCHES CLINICAL TRIAL TO TEST ANTIBODY TREATMENT IN HOSPITALIZED COVID-19 PATIENTS.NIH - ACTIV-3 STUDY WILL BEGIN BY STUDYING INVESTIGATIONAL MONOCLONAL ANTIBODY LY-COV555.NIH - PHASE 3 RANDOMIZED, CONTROLLED TRIAL IS KNOWN AS ACTIV-3.NIH - INITIAL STAGE OF TRIAL AIMS TO ENROLL ABOUT 300 VOLUNTEERS HOSPITALIZED WITH MILD TO MODERATE COVID-19 WITH LESS THAN 13 DAYS OF SYMPTOMS.NIH - PARTICIPANTS ALSO WILL RECEIVE STANDARD CARE FOR COVID-19, INCLUDING ANTIVIRAL REMDESIVIR.NIH -  IF LY-COV555 APPEARS TO BE SAFE AND APPEARS TO BE EFFECTIVE, TRIAL WILL ENROLL ADDITIONAL 700 PARTICIPANTS.'}